 "Jawaharlal Nehru, a highly educated and charismatic leader, served as the primary political face of the Indian National Congress, articulating the vision for a modern, secular India.",
 "Muhammad Ali Jinnah emerged as the resolute advocate for the political and cultural rights of the Muslim minority, increasingly championing separate political representation.",
 "Sardar Vallabhbhai Patel played an indispensable, pragmatic role in the complex and delicate political maneuvering required to integrate hundreds of semi-autonomous princely states into the new Indian Union."
